msgid "options_video_animation_reduction_per_meter"
msgstr "Reduction of animation quality per meter. (inactive)"

msgid "options_video_animation_reduction_per_meter_tooltip"
msgstr "Has no effect at present - see Enable quality reduction of animations."

msgid "options_video_animation_reduction_per_meter_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: none"

msgid "options_video_animation_reduction_start"
msgstr "Minimum distance to start animation quality reduction. (inactive)"

msgid "options_video_animation_reduction_start_tooltip"
msgstr "Has no effect at present - see Enable quality reduction of animations."

msgid "options_video_animation_reduction_start_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: none"

msgid "options_video_antialiasing_quality"
msgstr "Anti-Aliasing (Supersampling): %1"

msgid "options_video_antialiasing_quality_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Smooths jagged edges by rendering the scene larger than your screen and "
"shrinking it down. This is the single most expensive setting in the game: "
"measured in a field test, 2x cost about 1.5ms a frame while 4x cost around "
"14ms - roughly three quarters of the frame rate. Use FXAA instead if you "
"want smooth edges cheaply."

msgid "options_video_antialiasing_quality_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: 2x medium, 4x MAJOR"

msgid "options_video_antialiasing_tier_1_5x"
msgstr "1.5x"

msgid "options_video_antialiasing_tier_2x"
msgstr "2x"

msgid "options_video_antialiasing_tier_4x"
msgstr "4x"

msgid "options_video_antialiasing_tier_off"
msgstr "Off"

msgid "options_video_auto_optimize"
msgstr "Enable Auto Optimization."

msgid "options_video_auto_optimize_target_fps"
msgstr "If FPS drop below %1 Auto Optimization will kick in."

msgid "options_video_auto_optimize_target_fps_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"The frame rate Auto Optimization tries to hold. It only does anything while "
"Enable Auto Optimization is ticked."

msgid "options_video_auto_optimize_target_fps_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: sets the target, no cost of its own"

msgid "options_video_auto_optimize_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Watches your frame rate and, when it falls below the figure set underneath, "
"automatically becomes more aggressive about not drawing small distant "
"objects. It relaxes again once the frame rate recovers."

msgid "options_video_auto_optimize_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: helps when struggling, costs nothing otherwise"

msgid "options_video_background_frame_cap"
msgstr "Limit frame rate while the game is in the background (30 fps)"

msgid "options_video_background_frame_cap_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Caps the frame rate to 30 while the game window is not focused, so the card "
"is not running flat out for a window you are not looking at. Leave this on "
"unless you are measuring performance, since it will hold you at 30 whenever "
"you alt-tab away."

msgid "options_video_background_frame_cap_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: a saving while in the background"

msgid "options_video_defaults_confirmation"
msgstr "Are you sure you want to reset all Video settings to their defaults?"

msgid "options_video_display_mode"
msgstr "Select Display Mode"

msgid "options_video_display_mode_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Full screen and windowed allow resolution changes. Borderless window mode "
"does not currently allow this."

msgid "options_video_display_mode_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: none"

msgid "options_video_displaymodelist"
msgstr "Select display resolution."

msgid "options_video_enable_animation_reduction"
msgstr "Enable quality reduction of animations. (inactive - no effect)"

msgid "options_video_enable_animation_reduction_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Has no effect at present. The setting is stored and remembered, but nothing "
"reads it, so animations are not reduced at any distance."

msgid "options_video_enable_animation_reduction_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: none"

msgid "options_video_enable_antialiasing"
msgstr "Enable antialiasing."

msgid "options_video_enable_character_shadows"
msgstr "Enable Character Shadows."

msgid "options_video_enable_character_shadows_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Whether players, mounts and monsters cast shadows. Cheaper than scenery "
"shadows in most places, but rises with the number of characters on screen, "
"so it costs most in a crowded fight."

msgid "options_video_enable_character_shadows_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: medium"

msgid "options_video_enable_drop_shadows"
msgstr "Enable Drop Shadows (inactive - no effect)"

msgid "options_video_enable_drop_shadows_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Has no effect at present. The drop shadow system is still built and kept "
"alive, but the call that would draw it is commented out in the renderer, so "
"toggling this changes nothing you can see."

msgid "options_video_enable_drop_shadows_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: none"

msgid "options_video_enable_filmic_tone"
msgstr "Enable Filmic Tone Mapping"

msgid "options_video_enable_filmic_tone_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Applies a film-like curve to the final image, pulling back blown-out "
"highlights and deepening shadows rather than clipping them."

msgid "options_video_enable_filmic_tone_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: minor"

msgid "options_video_enable_fxaa"
msgstr "Enable FXAA (fast antialiasing)."

msgid "options_video_enable_fxaa_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"A cheap edge smoothing pass applied after the scene is drawn. Much softer in "
"effect than supersampling, and nearly free - it is the sensible choice on "
"most machines."

msgid "options_video_enable_fxaa_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: minimal"

msgid "options_video_enable_godrays"
msgstr "Enable God Rays"

msgid "options_video_enable_godrays_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Visible shafts of light through gaps in geometry, such as sun through trees "
"or a doorway."

msgid "options_video_enable_godrays_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: medium"

msgid "options_video_enable_post_process_effects"
msgstr "Enable Post Process Effects."

msgid "options_video_enable_post_process_effects_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"The master switch for screen-space effects applied after the world is drawn, "
"such as tone mapping and god rays. Turning it off skips that whole stage."

msgid "options_video_enable_post_process_effects_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: medium"

msgid "options_video_enable_scenery_shadows"
msgstr "Enable Scenery Shadows."

msgid "options_video_enable_scenery_shadows_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Whether world geometry - buildings, trees, terrain features - casts shadows. "
"Usually the larger half of the shadow cost, since there is far more scenery "
"than there are characters."

msgid "options_video_enable_scenery_shadows_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: medium to major"

msgid "options_video_enable_shadows"
msgstr "Enable Shadows."

msgid "options_video_enable_shadows_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"The master switch for shadows cast into the world. Turning this off removes "
"the whole shadow pass and is one of the largest single savings available, at "
"an obvious cost to how the world looks."

msgid "options_video_enable_shadows_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: major"

msgid "options_video_enable_ssao"
msgstr "Enable Ambient Occlusion (SSAO)"

msgid "options_video_enable_ssao_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Adds soft contact shadowing where surfaces meet - under eaves, in corners, "
"where objects touch the ground. Adds depth without affecting real shadows."

msgid "options_video_enable_ssao_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: minor"

msgid "options_video_enable_triple_buffering"
msgstr "Enable triple buffering."

msgid "options_video_enable_triple_buffering_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Only has any effect while vertical sync is enabled, where it smooths out "
"frames that miss the refresh, at the cost of slightly more input delay."

msgid "options_video_enable_triple_buffering_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: negligible"

msgid "options_video_filmic_tone_strength"
msgstr "Filmic Tone Mapping Strength: %1"

msgid "options_video_filmic_tone_strength_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"How strongly the filmic curve is applied. Higher means more contrast and a "
"stronger rolloff in bright areas; lower keeps the image closer to how the "
"engine rendered it. Purely a look preference."

msgid "options_video_filmic_tone_strength_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: none beyond the effect itself"

msgid "options_video_fov"
msgstr "Field of View: %1"

msgid "options_video_fov_tooltip"
msgstr "Widens the player's view."

msgid "options_video_fov_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: negligible"

msgid "options_video_gamma_correction"
msgstr "Gamma Correction: %1"

msgid "options_video_gamma_correction_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Brightens or darkens the whole image. Only works in full screen - Windows "
"ignores the gamma ramp in windowed and borderless modes."

msgid "options_video_gamma_correction_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: none"

msgid "options_video_godray_intensity"
msgstr "God Ray Intensity: %1"

msgid "options_video_godray_intensity_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"How pronounced the light shafts are. Changes the look rather than the amount "
"of work, so the cost is in having God Rays enabled at all."

msgid "options_video_godray_intensity_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: none beyond the effect itself"

msgid "options_video_label_resolution"
msgstr "Screen resolution"

msgid "options_video_legacy_third_person_camera"
msgstr "Legacy 3rd person camera"

msgid "options_video_maxnumbloodstains"
msgstr "Maximum Number of Bloodstains: %1"

msgid "options_video_maxnumdynamiclight"
msgstr "Maximum Number of Dynamic Lights: %1"

msgid "options_video_maxnumdynamiclight_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"How many nearby light sources - torches, lava, spells - can light the world "
"at once. Only lights within about 350m of you count toward this, so empty "
"areas cost nothing. Note that the cost rises with supersampling, because the "
"lighting pass runs at the enlarged resolution."

msgid "options_video_maxnumdynamiclight_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: medium"

msgid "options_video_maxnumparticles"
msgstr "Maximum Number of Particle Effects: %1"

msgid "options_video_maxnumparticles_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"How many particle effects can run at once - spell impacts, fire, blood, "
"weather. Costs nothing while nothing is happening, and most during a busy "
"fight, so lowering it mainly helps in the moments where frame rate matters "
"most."

msgid "options_video_maxnumparticles_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: minor when quiet, higher in heavy combat"

msgid "options_video_object_clipping"
msgstr "Enable Object Clipping"

msgid "options_video_object_clipping_max_function_value"
msgstr "Maximum function value to clip (Lower value=bigger chance to clip)."

msgid "options_video_object_clipping_max_function_value_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"How aggressively objects are clipped. A lower value clips more, at the cost "
"of objects disappearing closer to you. Only applies while Object Clipping is "
"enabled."

msgid "options_video_object_clipping_max_function_value_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: lower saves more"

msgid "options_video_object_clipping_max_size_to_clip"
msgstr "Maximum Size of object to clip."

msgid "options_video_object_clipping_max_size_to_clip_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Objects larger than this are never clipped, however far away they are, so "
"that landmarks and buildings do not vanish. Only applies while Object "
"Clipping is enabled."

msgid "options_video_object_clipping_max_size_to_clip_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: higher clips more, so saves more"

msgid "options_video_object_clipping_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Stops drawing objects once they are small enough on screen not to be missed "
"- a crate at a distance rather than a building. One of the cheapest ways to "
"buy frame rate, and on by default."

msgid "options_video_object_clipping_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: a saving - turning this OFF costs frame rate"

msgid "options_video_object_min_distance_to_clip"
msgstr ""
"Minimum distance an object has to be before it can potentially clipped."

msgid "options_video_object_min_distance_to_clip_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Nothing closer to you than this is ever clipped, so objects never vanish "
"from under your feet. Only applies while Object Clipping is enabled."

msgid "options_video_object_min_distance_to_clip_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: lower saves more"

msgid "options_video_preset_max"
msgstr "Max"

msgid "options_video_preset_max_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Everything at maximum except supersampling, which no preset turns on - set "
"it yourself under Anti-Aliasing (Supersampling) on the Effects tab if you "
"have frames to spare. If this is too heavy, these are the settings that cost "
"the most, in order - turn them down before anything else:"

msgid "options_video_preset_max_tooltip_2"
msgstr ""
"1. Enable Shadows and Shadow Quality - Lighting tab. Scenery shadows are the "
"larger half."

msgid "options_video_preset_max_tooltip_3"
msgstr ""
"2. Maximum Number of Dynamic Lights - Lighting tab. Costs more while "
"supersampling is on."

msgid "options_video_preset_max_tooltip_4"
msgstr ""
"3. Vegetation Density and Area Size - Quality tab. A smaller area costs "
"MORE, not less."

msgid "options_video_preset_max_tooltip_5"
msgstr "4. View Distance - Performance tab. Matters most on open terrain."

msgid "options_video_preset_max_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: very demanding"

msgid "options_video_preset_medium"
msgstr "Medium"

msgid "options_video_preset_medium_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"The recommended setting. Shadows, lighting and effects on at sensible "
"quality, with FXAA smoothing the edges and supersampling left off. This is "
"what most machines should run."

msgid "options_video_preset_medium_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: balanced"

msgid "options_video_preset_minimum"
msgstr "Minimum"

msgid "options_video_preset_minimum_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Everything at its cheapest: no supersampling, no shadows, no dynamic lights, "
"minimal vegetation and effects off. FXAA stays on because it smooths edges "
"for almost nothing. For the lowest-end machines, or when you want every "
"frame you can get."

msgid "options_video_preset_minimum_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: fastest"

msgid "options_video_shader_version"
msgstr "Select Shader Version"

msgid "options_video_shadow_quality"
msgstr "Select Quality of Shadows"

msgid "options_video_shadow_quality_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"The resolution of the shadow map, from 1024 at Low up to 8192 at Max. Higher "
"means crisper shadow edges rather than blocky ones; each step up quadruples "
"the number of shadow pixels drawn."

msgid "options_video_shadow_quality_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: medium to major at the top end"

msgid "options_video_shadow_smoothing"
msgstr "Select Quality of Shadowsmoothing"

msgid "options_video_shadow_smoothing_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"How much work goes into softening the edge of a shadow. Higher settings "
"sample the shadow map more times per pixel, trading frame rate for edges "
"that look soft instead of jagged."

msgid "options_video_shadow_smoothing_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: medium"

msgid "options_video_tab_display"
msgstr "Display"

msgid "options_video_tab_effects"
msgstr "Effects"

msgid "options_video_tab_lighting"
msgstr "Lighting"

msgid "options_video_tab_performance"
msgstr "Performance"

msgid "options_video_tab_quality"
msgstr "Quality"

msgid "options_video_texture_anisotropy_level"
msgstr "Select Texture Anisotropy Level"

msgid "options_video_texture_anisotropy_level_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"How sharp textures stay when viewed at a steep angle, such as ground "
"stretching away from you. Higher keeps detail out to the horizon instead of "
"blurring into mush a few paces ahead. Only applies while Texture Filtering "
"is set to Anisotropic."

msgid "options_video_texture_anisotropy_level_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: minor"

msgid "options_video_texture_filtering"
msgstr "Select Texture Filtering"

msgid "options_video_texture_filtering_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"How textures are sampled and blended between detail levels. Anisotropic is "
"the sharpest and is the recommended setting."

msgid "options_video_texture_filtering_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: minor"

msgid "options_video_texture_quality"
msgstr "Select Texture Quality (inactive - no effect)"

msgid "options_video_texture_quality_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Has no effect at present. The setting is stored and remembered, but never "
"reaches the renderer, so changing it will not alter how the game looks or "
"runs."

msgid "options_video_texture_quality_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: none"

msgid "options_video_vegetation_area_size"
msgstr "Vegetation Area Size: %1"

msgid "options_video_vegetation_area_size_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"The radius that grass is scattered over. This works together with Vegetation "
"Density: the number of plants is capped, so a SMALLER area packs that same "
"number closer to you - thicker grass, and a heavier load because more of it "
"fills the screen. A larger area spreads the plants thinner but draws them "
"further into the distance."

msgid "options_video_vegetation_area_size_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: major - LOWER values cost more"

msgid "options_video_vegetation_density"
msgstr "Vegetation Density: %1"

msgid "options_video_vegetation_density_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"How many plants are scattered. This works together with Vegetation Area "
"Size: more plants is a heavier load, and at the maximum the scatter stops "
"placing any extra ones, so going higher would only cost memory. Combine with "
"a small area for thick grass close by, or a large area for sparse grass that "
"reaches further."

msgid "options_video_vegetation_density_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: major - HIGHER values cost more"

msgid "options_video_view_distance"
msgstr "View Distance: %1 m"

msgid "options_video_view_distance_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"How far into the distance the world is drawn. The cost depends heavily on "
"where you are - open terrain with a long sightline is far more expensive "
"than a dungeon or a city street."

msgid "options_video_view_distance_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: medium, and varies by location"

msgid "options_video_wait_for_vsync"
msgstr "Wait for vertical sync on monitor."

msgid "options_video_wait_for_vsync_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Matches the frame rate to your monitor's refresh rate, removing the "
"horizontal tearing you see when the two drift apart. Costs a little input "
"delay, and caps your frame rate at the refresh rate."

msgid "options_video_wait_for_vsync_tooltip_perf"
msgstr "Performance: minor"

msgid "options_window_title"
msgstr "Options"

msgid "paperdoll_auto_eat_options_tooltip"
msgstr "Auto-eat options"

msgid "paperdoll_button_get_naked"
msgstr "Get Naked"

msgid "paperdoll_button_refresh"
msgstr "Refresh"

msgid "paperdoll_button_unequip_all"
msgstr "Unequip All"

msgid "paperdoll_button_unequip_all_tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Takes off your armor, robe, clothing, cape and jewelry (only while you wear "
"armor). Weapons, ammo and the utility slots stay equipped. Instant at a bank "
"out of combat, otherwise after 20 seconds."

msgid "paperdoll_effect_modifier_1"
msgstr "Obelisk of Ragunius"

msgid "paperdoll_effect_modifier_2"
msgstr "Clan land villages defensive PVE bonus"

msgid "paperdoll_effect_modifier_3"
msgstr "Clan land villages offensive PVE bonus"

msgid "paperdoll_effect_modifier_4"
msgstr "Clan sea villages defensive PVE bonus"

msgid "paperdoll_effect_modifier_5"
msgstr "Clan sea villages offensive PVE bonus"

msgid "paperdoll_effect_modifier_6"
msgstr "Clan sea villages offensive siege bonus"

msgid "paperdoll_enchantment_more"
msgstr "+%1 more"

msgid "paperdoll_enchantment_none"
msgstr "No enchantments on your gear"

msgid "paperdoll_enchantment_not_applied"
msgstr "not applied"

msgid "paperdoll_header_clan"
msgstr "Clan: %1"

msgid "paperdoll_info_armor"
msgstr ""
"Only the helmet and the chest piece can be enchanted, and like enchantments "
"do not combine: with two Strength enchantments, only the stronger one "
"applies. A robe replaces your armor: putting one on takes off everything you "
"wear, and its hood goes in the helmet slot."

msgid "paperdoll_info_armor_penalties"
msgstr ""
"How your worn armor holds you back. Encumbrance comes from what you wear. "
"Melee, Magic and Archery show the encumbrance at which each starts to "
"suffer. Hover a row for details."

msgid "paperdoll_info_base_attributes"
msgstr ""
"Your six base attributes. Spend unspent attribute points with the + beside "
"one; Shift-click spends 5. Hover an attribute to see what it does."

msgid "paperdoll_info_clothing"
msgstr ""
"Clothing and jewelry are worn under your armor. They mainly reduce the "
"damage your other equipped armor takes. A robe takes them off too."

msgid "paperdoll_info_enchantments"
msgstr ""
"The enchantments on what you wear. Like enchantments do not combine: when "
"two raise the same stat, only the stronger applies, and the weaker one is "
"shown as not applied. Crafted enchantments add up."

msgid "paperdoll_info_protections"
msgstr ""
"How much each kind of damage is reduced by your armor and effects: physical "
"damage, the magic schools and afflictions. Hover a row for details."

msgid "paperdoll_info_talismans"
msgstr ""
"The first slot takes a rune book or a talisman. The second and third take "
"talismans and are bought from Slayer Master Aero."

msgid "paperdoll_info_utility"
msgstr ""
"Figurine: a mount, ship or warhulk figurine. Loot Bag: items you loot with a "
"click go into this bag. Food: eaten by itself whenever your meal runs out, "
"while Auto-eat is ticked. The cog sets the Auto-eat key."

msgid "paperdoll_info_weapons"
msgstr ""
"Main hand, shield and ammunition. A two-handed, dual-wielded or tool weapon "
"leaves no room for a shield."

msgid "paperdoll_item_attached_at"
msgstr "Attached at %1"

msgid "paperdoll_label_ammo"
msgstr "Ammo"

msgid "paperdoll_label_auto_eat"
msgstr "Auto-eat"

msgid "paperdoll_label_cape"
msgstr "Cape"

msgid "paperdoll_label_character_id"
msgstr "Character ID: %1"

msgid "paperdoll_label_equipment_tier"
